WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:04.680
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.020
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.150
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.950
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.010
<i>Brilliant, brilliant.</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.350
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:04.220
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:22.020
Don't just stand there.
If you want something, come in.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.580
I see.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:30.330
The formidable sword of Kondou Isami, 
the fearsome commander of the Shinsengumi,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.370
isn't all that impressive, is he?

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.710
That's why I'm training like this.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.410
I can't be dragging everyone down.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.420
Sakamoto Ryouma and Kondou Isami.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.530
The man who brought down the shogunate, 
and the man who protected it.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:56.440
To think the swords of former enemies
 would be reunited in the flesh like this.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:03.110
If you haven't finished training yet, 
how about some gun training with me?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:09.450
I don't know anything beyond the manly, 
direct sword style of Kondou Isami!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.330
Thus, I strive to be loyal to 
this method of fighting!

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:20.470
Hey now, Sakamoto Ryouma is 
the definition of manly!

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.050
Sakamoto was cheerful and openhearted!

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.050
<b>Cheerful and 
Openhearted</b>

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:29.350
No, Kondou Isami was more 
forthright in his manliness!

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.350
<b>Forthright</b>

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.670
Sakamoto was broadminded!

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.550
Kondou was incredibly generous!

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.020
He was affable!

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.350
He was indomitable!

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.350
He was gentle but firm!

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.980
He was enterprising and daring!

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:40.910
Sakamoto!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.170
Kondou!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.650
Do those two not get along?

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.330
Or is it the opposite?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.610
They get along because they don't get along.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.960
I see. It's complicated.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.370
Kondou!

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.620
Sakamoto!

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.620
Kondou!

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.930
Now that fall has ended, winter begins.
 Loneliness hangs in the air, does it not?

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.270
You think so?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.240
I thought you liked summer, Urashima, 
but do you like winter as well?

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.940
That's not it, Hachisuka-niichan!

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.780
It's because Nagasone-niichan 
has arrived at the citadel!

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.680
I'm so glad all of us 
siblings are together.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.620
I even got to train with 
Nagasone-niichan yesterday.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.360
And he didn't go easy on me!

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.680
How unpleasant.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:45.120
Nagasone-niichan's gotten so 
strong already! He's amazing!

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.660
That man is not your older 
brother, nor anything close.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.880
He's a fake calling himself a Kotetsu.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:57.680
Like I could ever get along with a forgery.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.900
That doesn't matter to me, though.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.360
Whether he's authentic or a forgery...

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.970
Master, they've appeared there again?

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.330
The Sword Warriors being dispatched are—

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.310
Very well, these six?

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:24.260
They should be able to fulfill their duty.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.300
Dispatch orders have come 
from Master for you all.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.330
Do not be alarmed, and calmly listen to me.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:39.670
Somehow!

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.020
The History Retrograde Army has...

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.270
...infiltrated the Ikeda Inn again, right?

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.530
What, you were already prepared?

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:54.650
I mean, given that you gathered the five 
Shinsengumi swords, it had to be that.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.760
You're being sent to the Ikeda 
Inn in Kyoto in the year 1864.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.730
These five swords are going?

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.750
No, there's one more.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.290
Looks like I'll be going with 
you guys to the Ikeda Inn.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.320
I have no idea what our Master is thinking.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.460
So it's you.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.570
Surely there's some intention behind it.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.360
Knock off the fighting and 
dragging out the relationship

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.060
between your former masters.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.100
It's an indoor battle in narrow rooms.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:26.150
Cooperate and fight together, so you're 
not just slashing around recklessly.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:30.080
Cooperate? I wonder if he can manage that?

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.270
Oh, scary.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.350
The captain is Yamatonokami Yasusada.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.580
Y-Yes.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.770
Captain, huh? I'm counting on you.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.040
I'll help you, too!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:49.470
Sword Protection Charm

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.030
Yamatonokami, this is from Master.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:49.480
A protection charm?

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:54.940
As Master's attendant, I'm always
 by their side, so I know this much.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.710
You had a fierce fight at the Ikeda Inn.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:00.870
Master knows how hard 
you've worked since then.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.550
They've been keeping a close eye on you.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.470
Show them the fruits of your labor.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:07.910
What?

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.820
They've only been watching Yasusada?

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.050
Master always keeps an eye 
on everyone, of course.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:16.770
They've been enjoying your 
stories as well, Kashuu.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:22.160
Master cares about all the Sword 
Warriors that are gathered here.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:26.130
Return the sentiment, Yamatonokami.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.620
What's the matter?

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.230
I just got nervous all of a sudden.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:38.970
In that case, Master entrusted
 me to give you this.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.970
What? That's so nice.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:42.690
What is this box?

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.780
Is there something inside it?

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.650
Who knows? I'm not sure.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.280
I'm going to open it.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:51.360
<b>"Sa"</b>

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.870
Ouch!

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.580
It's a jack-in-the-box.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:04.510
Your nervousness is gone now, isn't it?

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:05.280
Yeah!

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.740
This is another part of Master's kindness.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:11.280
All right, you are being 
dispatched in 30 minutes.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.540
Before we go,

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.190
I want to come up with a battle strategy,

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.170
so can we all gather in the great room?

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:22.220
I've been over the tactics in my 
head numerous times since that day.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.750
Kashuu, do you have a minute?

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.650
What is it?

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:34.590
Master has high hopes for Yamatonokami.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:38.370
However, I'm honestly concerned.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.270
He strongly adores Okita Souji—

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:42.950
That's...

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:46.660
all in the past now.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.230
Is it really?

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:52.970
Okita Souji isn't the one who 
is wielding us anymore now.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.140
<b>"Sa"</b>

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:54.750
This is our Master now.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.130
Yasusada knows that, too.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.330
He's not pushing himself, is he?

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:02.250
He's gotten stronger mentally as well.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.680
Believe in him.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.590
Kashuu, I'm counting on you.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.640
I know.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Reception Room

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Dirt Floor

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Dirt Floor
Well

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Well 
Kitchen

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Front Stairs

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Dining Room

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Front Stairs

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.780
Courtyard

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:21.750
What is the History Retrograde Army's 
goal in going to the Ikeda Inn?

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:26.200
Attack the Shinsengumi and keep the 
anti-shogunate ronin alive, perhaps?

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:31.880
Makes sense. By keeping them alive, 
they'll turn Kyoto into a sea of fire.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.930
That's how they want to alter history, huh?

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.440
Probably, it seems the most likely.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:41.850
So, the History Retrograde Army will be 
supporting the anti-shogunate ronin.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.710
They'll be lying in wait, either 
hiding in the Ikeda Inn

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.890
or nearby until the Shinsengumi arrive.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:50.260
How shall we fight them, then, Yamatonokami?

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:55.740
On that day, the Shinsengumi split into 
the Kondou unit and the Hijikata unit,

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.280
searching for the anti-shogunate ronin 
lurking somewhere in the city of Kyoto.

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:04.660
During the search, the Kondou unit saw 
the ronin as they entered the Inn.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:10.540
Four of them: Kondou, Okita, Nagakura, and 
Toudou stormed the Inn from the front.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.440
Right?

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:12.760
Yeah.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.340
I remember it well.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:18.010
When they fought on the second floor, 
they found the anti-shogunate ronin.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:27.250
Back Stairs

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:28.980
Second Floor

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:28.980
Courtyard

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:28.980
Front Stairs

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:28.980
Dining Room

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:28.980
Courtyard

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:28.980
Front Stairs

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:23.790
If we can, we should lure the Retrograde 
Army to the first floor or the backyard.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.980
Kitchen

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.010
Worst case, we fight in hiding even 
if they go up to the second floor.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.980
Well

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.980
Dirt Floor

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.590
We will split up into two groups.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:36.070
Nagasone-san, Mutsunokami, Kiyomitsu, 
and myself will storm the entrance.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:39.560
Izuminokami and Horikawa will 
fight in the back yard.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:42.060
We'll make the enemy think that you're the Shinsengumi with your haori,

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.710
and lure them to the backyard.

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:45.790
Okay, got it.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.630
Oh, so I'm with Nagasone, then?

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.080
The gun is stronger than the sword.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:55.910
Fight with me and you'll quickly find out 
why they call it the age of handgun.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:00.000
Will you be able to say the same 
thing after seeing me work?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:04.950
Now, now. Like Hasebe said, we have 
to cooperate and fight together.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.090
When we're done, we'll meet up on the roof.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.440
On the roof?

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.310
No one will come up there.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.640
All right, good luck, everyone!

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:16.610
Got it!

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:16.610
Yeah!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:25.070
Okay, Kane-san, you look cool.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.800
Do you remember this?

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.760
That's the one I gave you.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.580
I will never fight that selfishly 
and carelessly again.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.470
You're going like that?

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.270
It's my reminder.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.110
We still have some time. Got a second?

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.490
There's one here, too!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:04.860
And here, too!

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.920
The flowers are blooming!

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:08.570
Flowers?

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:12.890
Yes, even though it's nearly winter, 
the cherry blossoms have bloomed.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.650
Huh?!

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:14.540
Really?

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.640
I'm glad to be able to see the cherry
blossoms with my little brothers

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:19.750
without having to wait for spring.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.340
I-I'm glad, too!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:26.330
What kind of tree has cherry blossoms
 that bloom even in the winter?

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.820
We thought that it was a "ten
thousand leaf cherry tree,"

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:31.060
but we're not so sure anymore.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:35.930
Only this tree knows what it is thinking.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:40.020
What we <i>do</i> know is that this 
tree doesn't want to bore us.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.640
Hey, do you remember this?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.150
That...

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:55.120
Why do you have that paper?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:13:02.590
<b>I will protect Okita-kun.</b>

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.000
I knew we'd eventually
 return to the Ikeda Inn.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.220
I thought I'd show you 
this when the time came.

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:04.760
Are you still having that dream?

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:09.790
The one where you're the sword 
he took to the Ikeda Inn, not me?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.750
Yeah.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:14.530
Sometimes.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:19.640
I looked up to Okita-kun, and
 I still care about him even now.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:25.130
But, I'm different than I was 
when I first arrived here.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.370
I've had a change of heart.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:33.810
I'm fighting for the sake of 
our Master and this citadel.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.230
Look in my eyes.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.690
You don't need that anymore, then.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.640
So the protection charm will be empty?

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.960
It's fine, because I have this.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:58.010
I like it, since it's pretty.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.270
When these cherry blossoms 
bloom splendidly again,

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:06.390
I'd like to have Master 
enjoy them without worry.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:11.800
For that to happen, do all you 
can to return with smiles.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:15.250
<b>Sincerity</b>

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.620
Yes, we leave the Hanamaru to you.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.530
Good luck.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:17.820
Do your best.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.460
Otegine

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:21.900
Please do your best!

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:22.460
Yeah!

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:24.420
Good luck!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.780
I won't forgive you if you break.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:37.140
Right.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.480
All right then, let's liven 
things up. How about a drink?

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.190
I would like to drink some tea.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.130
Nakigitsune! Will you make some inari zushi?

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:49.560
I'll bring some candy!

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:51.880
Hey! Are you all trying to have a party?

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:55.050
They're all about to leave on a vital
 mission! Have some restraint!

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:59.150
What? <i>We</i> aren't going, though.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.290
Come now, Hasebe-kun.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:03.510
This is just our way of doing things.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:08.130
There's no dissuading you guys.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.900
Okay, time for party preparations!

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:12.720
Yeah!

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.890
We'll be off to the Ikeda Inn, then!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.980
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:28.990
<b>Evening of June 5th, 1864 - Kyoto</b>

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.460
As we planned, we split into two groups.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.270
We'll go the backyard.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.740
Let's go, Kane-san.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.370
Show us your cool side.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.460
Who do you think I am?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.970
Ikeda Inn

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:04.330
Will you let me open the door?

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.150
Let's go.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:18.490
<b>Sincerity</b>

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.420
There's a bunch of them.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:25.310
Such a grand welcome.

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.790
It's tough being popular.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.170
Don't say stupid things! Take this seriously.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.690
I know.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:34.990
I'm not responsible if you're
 careless and break or shatter.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.380
That's not very appealing.

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:41.010
I guess I'll get serious.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.370
Got no choice, do I?

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:58.900
This way!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.710
Hey, Kunihiro...

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.660
Isn't this a few too many?

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:10.200
I'll show you the three-step thrust

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.410
that I practiced with Kiyomitsu!

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:27.270
This isn't even a wound.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.520
Lose your head and die!

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.620
Amazing, Kane-san!

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.830
You don't have to say that every time.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.760
Fighting one-on-one?

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.300
Don't go up there!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:02.540
Yasusada!

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:03.920
I'm going up to the second floor!

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:05.510
Don't let the ronin see you!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.470
<i>Don't get broken on the second floor!</i>

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:13.260
What was that sound?

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:20.940
There's no one there.

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:30.050
So you're the boss?

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:36.670
Kunihiro!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.220
You've really done it now!

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.430
Now, Kunihiro!

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.250
Right, Kane-san!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.220
Double Sword...

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:52.760
...Attack!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.570
Job well done.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:08.700
You too, Kane-san!

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.760
I was serious this time.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:34.520
A bit closer and you would've cut me, too.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.830
Even you would've been able to avoid that.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:56.260
Thanks.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.010
That makes us even.

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.390
Are there any left?

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:20.870
Yamatonokami is facing 
off with the last one.

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:22.720
He'll be fine.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:25.190
We can't stay here.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.110
The Shinsengumi are coming.

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:28.690
Let's go up to the roof!

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:39.400
One bold Okita strike!

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.250
Hey, you.

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:15.120
I've never seen you before, are you new?

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:21.860
That sword looks like
a splendid piece of work.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:22.950
Ah, this...

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:26.490
If you aren't going to use that sword now,
just when do you plan on using it?

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:30.840
Come on!

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:32.050
W-Wait!

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.980
This is a Shinsengumi raid!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.050
The Shinsengumi have arrived.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:41.740
So it's started.

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:44.480
Damn, Yasusada is late.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:56.120
Okita-kun!

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:00.340
Stop!

00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:16.720
<i>Okita-kun!</i>

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:00.030
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
